.SH "NAME"
(*econf\&.File)\&.<Type>, (*econf\&.File)\&.<Type>Def \- retrieve a value from an econf\&.File

.SH "SYNOPSIS"

.sp
.ft B
.nf
import "github\&.com/openSUSE/libeconf/go/econf"
.fi
.ft
.sp
.nf
\fBfunc (f *econf\&.File) Int(group, key string) (int32, error)\fR
\fBfunc (f *econf\&.File) IntDef(group, key string, def int32) (int32, error)\fR

\fBfunc (f *econf\&.File) Int64(group, key string) (int64, error)\fR
\fBfunc (f *econf\&.File) Int64Def(group, key string, def int64) (int64, error)\fR

\fBfunc (f *econf\&.File) UInt(group, key string) (uint32, error)\fR
\fBfunc (f *econf\&.File) UIntDef(group, key string, def uint32) (uint32, error)\fR

\fBfunc (f *econf\&.File) UInt64(group, key string) (uint64, error)\fR
\fBfunc (f *econf\&.File) UInt64Def(group, key string, def uint64) (uint64, error)\fR

\fBfunc (f *econf\&.File) Float(group, key string) (float32, error)\fR
\fBfunc (f *econf\&.File) FloatDef(group, key string, def float32) (float32, error)\fR

\fBfunc (f *econf\&.File) Double(group, key string) (float64, error)\fR
\fBfunc (f *econf\&.File) DoubleDef(group, key string, def float64) (float64, error)\fR

\fBfunc (f *econf\&.File) String(group, key string) (string, error)\fR
\fBfunc (f *econf\&.File) StringDef(group, key, def string) (string, error)\fR

\fBfunc (f *econf\&.File) Bool(group, key string) (bool, error)\fR
\fBfunc (f *econf\&.File) BoolDef(group, key string, def bool) (bool, error)\fR
.fi

.SH "DESCRIPTION"

.PP
These methods retrieve the value associated with a specific
\fIgroup\fR
and
\fIkey\fR
from the configuration file object
\fIf\fR, converted to the method's result type\&.

.PP
The
\fIgroup\fR
parameter specifies the section name in the configuration file\&. If
\fIgroup\fR
is
""\&, the key is looked up in the upper part of the file without any group
declaration\&. The
\fIkey\fR
parameter specifies the name of the entry to retrieve\&.

.PP
The
\fB\&.\&.\&.Def\fR
variants
(\fBIntDef\fR,
\fBInt64Def\fR,
\fBUIntDef\fR,
\fBUInt64Def\fR,
\fBFloatDef\fR,
\fBDoubleDef\fR,
\fBStringDef\fR,
\fBBoolDef\fR) return
\fIdef\fR
instead of an error when the
\fIgroup\fR/\fIkey\fR
combination is not found; any other error is still returned\&.

.PP
For
\fBBool\fR
and
\fBBoolDef\fR, common boolean strings (such as
"true",
"yes",
"1",
"false",
"no",
"0"
) are recognized irrespective of case\&.

.SH "RETURN VALUE"

.PP
On success, these methods return the converted value and a
\fInil\fR
error\&.

.PP
On failure, the non\-\fB\&.\&.\&.Def\fR
variants return the type's zero value and a non\-nil
\fI*econf\&.Error\fR
(see
\fBeconf_go_Error\fR(3))\&.

.PP
The
\fB\&.\&.\&.Def\fR
variants are wrappers that avoid having to check for
\fBeconf\&.ErrNoKey\fR
manually\&. If the
\fIgroup\fR/\fIkey\fR
combination is not found, they return
\fIdef\fR
together with
\fBeconf\&.ErrNoKey\fR
(callers that only care about missing keys can ignore this specific error
and use the returned
\fIdef\fR)\&. Any other error is returned together with the type's zero
value, as for the non\-\fB\&.\&.\&.Def\fR
variants\&.

.SH "ERRORS"

.PP
\fBeconf\&.ErrNoKey\fR
.RS 4
          The specified
\fIkey\fR
could not be found within the group\&. The
\fB\&.\&.\&.Def\fR
variants still return this error, together with
\fIdef\fR\&.
.RE

.PP
\fBeconf\&.ErrNoGroup\fR
.RS 4
          The specified
\fIgroup\fR
could not be found\&.
.RE

.PP
\fBeconf\&.ErrKeyHasNullValue\fR
.RS 4
          The given key has no value\&.
.RE

.PP
\fBeconf\&.ErrValueConversionError\fR
.RS 4
          The stored value cannot be converted to the requested type\&.
.RE

.PP
\fBeconf\&.ErrWrongBooleanValue\fR
.RS 4
          \fBBool\fR/\fBBoolDef\fR
only: the stored value is not a recognized boolean string\&.
.RE

.PP
\fBeconf\&.ErrNoMem\fR
.RS 4
          Memory allocation failed (specifically applicable to
\fBString\fR/\fBStringDef\fR)\&.
.RE

.SH "EXAMPLE"
.sp
.if n \{\
.RS 1
.\}
.nf

f, err := econf\&.ReadFile("/etc/example\&.conf", "=", "#")
if err != nil {
    log\&.Fatal(err)
}
defer f\&.Close()

count, err := f\&.Int("main", "count")
if err != nil {
    log\&.Fatal(err)
}

timeout, err := f\&.IntDef("main", "timeout", 30)
if err != nil && !errors\&.Is(err, econf\&.ErrNoKey) {
    log\&.Fatal(err)
}

.fi
.if n \{\
.RE
.\}
.sp

